        "a": "Yes. A press release written in news style uses the inverted pyramid: a headline, a dateline, a lead with the news in one sentence, supporting facts and a quote, then the boilerplate about the organization. Journalists skim releases from the top, so anything important that sits in paragraph five may never be read."
