        "a": "Most press releases run 300 to 500 words, about one page. That is enough for a headline, a one-sentence lead, the key facts, one or two quotes, a short boilerplate and a contact. If you need more, link to a fact sheet, report or study instead of adding paragraphs. Journalists read the top and decide in seconds."
