        "a": "Professional rapid reviews usually take days to a few weeks, compared with many months for a full systematic review. The time saved comes from narrowing the question, limiting databases and dates, and having one reviewer screen with a second checking a sample. AI speeds up screening and extraction, but not the judgment calls."
